            <ArticleTitle>[Acute ileitis due to Ascaris lumbricoides].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report their experience of two cases of acute ileitis with an obstructive complication due to &quot;Ascaris lumbricoides&quot;. The distinctive features were, in the first case, the pathogenic mechanism responsible of the occlusion, and in the second one, the need of a long term follow-up. The latter, especially in the &quot;aspecific forms&quot;, often allows an etiological diagnosis difficult even at laparotomy. Indicating the most frequent causes of surgical complications found in ileitis, which is a medical disease easily curable by medical and dietetic means, the authors confirm the difficulties of an etiological diagnosis and surgical treatment, increased by the rarity of the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
